// D10061: a `??` over an `i32 | null` list element with a runtime `f64` default is `i32 | f64`,
// as the same `??` over a parameter is (the numeric-join ruling). The proof tests `is i32`,
// which the checker refused as "can never match" while the element arm typed the result `f64`.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function __cjE(a: (i32 | null)[], d: f64) { return a[0] ?? d }
// @@VALUE@@
__cjE([5], 1.5)
// @@TYPE@@
i32 | f64
// @@TEST@@
v is i32
// @@HIT@@
print(v * 2)
// @@MISS@@
print("widened")
// @@WANT@@
10
// @@VALUE2@@
__cjE([null], 1.5)
// @@TYPE2@@
i32 | f64
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v)
// @@WANT2@@
1.5
